\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus still lead on
\par Till our rest be won
\par And, although the way be cheerless,
\par We will follow, calm and fearless:
\par Guide us by Thy hand 
\par To our Fatherland.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. If the way be drear,
\par If the foe be near,
\par Let not faithless fears o'ertake us,
\par Let not love and hope o'ertake us,
\par For through many a foe,
\par To our home we go.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When we seek relief
\par From a long-felt grief,
\par When oppressed by new temptations,
\par Lord increase and perfect patience:
\par Show us that bright shore
\par Where we weep no more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. When sweet earth and skies
\par Fade before our eyes;
\par When through death we look to heaven,
\par And our sins are all forgiven,
\par From Thy bright abode,
\par Call us home to God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jesus, still lead on,
\par Till our rest be won;
\par Heavenly Leader, still direct us,
\par Still support, console, protect us,
\par Till we safely stand
\par In our Fatherland.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

